}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mitama the Oracle''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Miko Mitama is usually much better in Evolved Form, but her Normal Form isn't terrible either, as she is basically a more defense-oriented [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]]. Thanks to her immunities, she is useful in stages with [[Kory]], [[Henry]], [[Croakley]] and other units that use these effects, but her low stats, long cooldown and short range prevent her from being anything more than an attacker with low impact and decent survivability to make up for it.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
The former queen of Uber Rares, Mitama the Oracle still remains an excellent support unit to this day. Her incredible Slow procs helps her have a strong impact in the vast majority of stages in the game.

Mitama the Oracle is a midranged support unit with a fair range of 350. But, thanks to [[Long Distance]], she can hit up to 650 range and has an amazing amount of pierce. This allows her to have wide coverage of the enemy frontline, dealing a surprisingly solid 4.2K DPS and more importantly, applies her devastating [[Slow|Slow]] proc. With it being a guaranteed proc that is applied to all Traited enemies (including Metal), has over 66% uptime (even higher with Fruit Treasures) and having aforementioned wide area coverage, this is one of the strongest control options in the game. Mitama the Oracle is also [[Resistant]] to Traited. This gives her a superb 148.7K HP against Traited enemies (119K without Fruit Treasures) at Lv.30, and this is paired with her 15 Knockbacks, giving her absurd amounts of staying power. Mitama's fast foreswing and full backswing also let her quickly retaliate when knocked back by a pusher, which is another strength. To top it all off, Mitama the Oracle is also immune to every debuff in the game at the time of her release (Knockback, Freeze, Slow, Weaken) alongside Wave Immunity, giving her even more versatility.

With this kit, Mitama the Oracle sees use in a majority of stages. If a stage is centred around aggressive Traited pushing power, Mitama's slow procs would trivialise it, rendering the enemy pushers sitting ducks. Indeed, Mitama the Oracle's competence at crippling pushers give her immaculate synergy with your ranged damage dealers, helping protect them and lock enemy frontliners in place for easy targeting. As the [[Stories of Legend]] mainly revolves around aggressive swarms and pushers, Mitama the Oracle would turn it into a joke if obtained at that point of time.

Mitama the Oracle is not without some flaws, however. She doesn't target Traitless, so her Slow and Resist are useless against them. Additionally, her standing range of 350 may not be long enough to hit certain enemies, requiring the use of stepping stones. Her high cost, long cooldown and slow speed are also annoying to work with. Furthermore, Mitama struggles into enemy snipers, such as [[Tackey]] and [[Mr. Mole]], who can hit her from a distance and abuse her slow speed and high knockback count.

Later on in the game, level design has not been kind to Mitama the Oracle, and this has knocked her down from the very top. Don't get it twisted, there are still stages starring Traited pushers, and you can absolutely count on Mitama to dominate them. However, many other stages have been moving towards synergistic enemy compositions rather than the brute force aggression as seen in the Stories of Legend. This also shifts the focus away from stacking groups of ranged damage dealers, which Mitama the Oracle works best with, to rushers and burst. [[Surge Attack|Surge]] and [[Explosion]] introduce new piercing threats to Mitama, such as [[Red EnerG]]. While Mitama's range lets her be safe from many Relic Enemies and their [[Curse|Curse]], she is rendered utterly useless if the user is not careful. This also makes ranged Curse applicants, such as [[Loris]] and [[Golem Sunfish]], her absolute bane. Many Aku Enemies also pack [[Aku Shield|Shields]] that can block Mitama's Slow procs, mandating the use of Shield Piercers against them.

Mitama the Oracle also faces heavy competition from [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Master of Life Dr. Nova]]. While Nova is unlocked very late into the game, and has worse Slow uptime, less knockbacks and lower (but still good) effective HP, Nova packs an immunity to Curse, patching up one of Mitama's flaws and has occasional Curse procs of her own. The biggest advantage Nova has over Mitama, however, is [[Sage Slayer]]. This allows her to bypass the debuff resistance of Sage Enemies, to whom Mitama the Oracle struggles heavily against, and thus see more usage in [[Zero Legends]].

However, even despite all these flaws, Mitama the Oracle still remains to be an excellent support unit, capable of applying powerful slow procs and see use all over the game, and is especially dominant early on in the game. She was not the former best Uber for nothing.

